    tier: "Octopus",
    erkennung: `The social Five wants to belong without losing herself: she seeks security not through practical withdrawal like the SE5, but through knowledge, systems, and connections that earn her a legitimate place in the group. In my book <em>Enneagramm Zoo</em> I describe the image of the <strong>Octopus</strong>, juggling books with all eight arms – knowledge becomes play, movement becomes thinking. She feels her way through the world cautiously, intelligently, in a controlled manner, watching closely who gives energy and who drains it.<br><br>Unlike the self-preservation Five, who withdraws physically, the SO5 stays present in the social field – but at a distance, as if underwater: calm, almost invisible, with an alert sense for every current. Anyone who understands this reads her analytical reserve not as disinterest, but as the attempt to earn a secure place in the community through understanding.`,
